# UNERA V2 — Stroked checkmark icon

Use the **same** checkmark geometry as the large success hero (`.success-icon-animated` / `.success-icon-animated-lg`) anywhere a **circular “done” chip** needs a check — not the Unicode character `✓`.

## Canonical markup

```html
<svg class="unera-checkmark" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg>
```

## Required CSS (path is stroked, not filled)

```css
.unera-checkmark {
  display: block;
  flex-shrink: 0;
  fill: none;
  stroke: currentColor;
  stroke-width: 3;
  stroke-linecap: round;
  stroke-linejoin: round;
}
```

Parent chips should set `color: white` (or equivalent) so `currentColor` matches the success surface — same pattern as `.success-icon-animated svg` / `.success-icon-animated-lg svg`.

## JS constant (static HTML demos)

Duplicate in each page’s script as needed:

```js
const UNERA_CHECKMARK_SVG = '<svg class="unera-checkmark" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg>';
```

Use `innerHTML = UNERA_CHECKMARK_SVG` for completed states; use `textContent = String(n)` for step numbers (clears SVG).

## Where this applies (`NewUnera/`)

| Surface | Selector / context |
|--------|---------------------|
| Desktop stepper | `#dynamicStepper .step.completed .step-circle` |
| Redeem tx tracker | `.ts-icon.ts-check` (processing + pending templates) |
| Get processing list | `.proc-icon.done` |

**Reference implementations:** `NewUnera/get-unera-cad.html`, `NewUnera/redeem-unera-cad.html`.

## Do not

- Do **not** use Unicode `✓` inside `.step-circle`, `.ts-icon.ts-check`, or `.proc-icon.done` — it will not match the success-screen stroke shape.
- Do **not** swap in a different path or stroke weight for these chips without updating **all** surfaces above and the large success SVG for visual parity.

## Out of scope

- **Copy-only** labels (e.g. “✓ Verified”, “✓ Rate updated”) may stay as text.
- **Pseudo-elements** with `content: '✓'` (e.g. mint path selected badge) need a different pattern if they must match this icon (real element or background SVG).
